T*
() Tj
T*
(Q1 - Virtual to physical address translation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(xv6 uses two-level paging. va2pa walks the calling process page table, checks that the PTE) Tj
T*
(is present and user-accessible, then combines the frame address with the 12-bit page offset.) Tj
T*
(It returns -1 for absent pages, supervisor-only pages, and addresses in the kernel range.) Tj
T*
(The kernel prints the page-directory index, page-table index, offset, and P/W/U flags.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(vatest requests translations for a global, local, and malloc-backed variable. It checks the) Tj
T*
(unmapped address 0x7fffffff and forks. Parent and child keep the same virtual address for) Tj
T*
(the global variable; copyuvm creates separate physical frames. Expected: equal VAs and) Tj
T*
(different PAs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Run: vatest) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
