(Q2 - Physical memory statistics) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(kalloc.c tracks the number of pages on the physical free list. kfree increments the count) Tj
T*
(and kalloc decrements it while kmem.lock is held during normal multiprocessor operation.) Tj
T*
(The bootstrap phase keeps xv6's lock-free initialization. ktotalpages reports the frames) Tj
T*
(managed by this allocator, excluding reserved memory and the kernel image.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The shared meminfo structure contains total_pages, free_pages, user_pages, and) Tj
T*
(page_table_pages. user_pages is sz / PGSIZE. page_table_pages counts the process page) Tj
T*
(directory and each present page-table page, including kernel mappings.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(memtest prints statistics before allocation, after it grows and touches two heap pages,) Tj
T*
(inside the forked child, and after the child is reaped. Expected: free pages decrease after) Tj
T*
(allocation and fork, then return to the post-allocation level after wait reclaims the child.) Tj
T*
(The test prints exact values during a QEMU run; no measured values are claimed here.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Runtime values to transcribe from memtest:) Tj
T*
(  Before allocation:       free_pages = \(capture from run\)) Tj
T*
(  After touching 2 pages:  free_pages = \(capture from run\)) Tj
T*
(  Child after fork:        free_pages = \(capture from run\)) Tj
T*
(  After wait:              free_pages = \(capture from run\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A free-list counter must cover both allocator initialization ranges and remain consistent) Tj
T*
(when child pages are released. Updating it at list insertion and removal keeps the count) Tj
T*
(aligned with the allocator's actual state.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Run: memtest) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
