(Q3 - Dumping the process page table) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(vmprint walks the process page directory. For each present user PDE it prints the page-table) Tj
T*
(physical address and flags. It then prints each present PTE with its virtual page, physical) Tj
T*
(frame, and P/W/U flags. Kernel mappings at or above KERNBASE are omitted from the detailed) Tj
T*
(dump and included in a one-line count.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(exec records the stack guard address while building a process image. vmprinttest prints the) Tj
T*
(expected guard VA so it can be found in the dump: the PTE is present \(P=1\) and inaccessible) Tj
T*
(to user mode \(U=0\). At startup, user-accessible pages should equal sz / PGSIZE minus the) Tj
T*
(guard page.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(vmprinttest captures the initial page table, reserves eight pages, touches one byte in each,) Tj
T*
(then prints again. It shrinks the heap by one page and prints a final dump. The touched) Tj
T*
(pages) Tj
T*
(should appear after growth and the final page should disappear after shrink. Empty page-) Tj
T*
(table) Tj
T*
(pages remain allocated until the address space is freed, matching xv6 deallocuvm behavior.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Because Q4 changes sbrk to lazy allocation, this test touches each reserved page before) Tj
T*
(checking the expanded dump.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Run: vmprinttest) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
