(Q4 - Lazy heap allocation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Positive sbrk extends proc->sz without allocating frames. Each process tracks heapbase and) Tj
T*
(stackguard. A page fault is resolved only for a missing page in the heap, below sz and above) Tj
T*
(the guard. The kernel allocates a zero-filled frame and maps it writable and user-) Tj
T*
(accessible.) Tj
T*
(Invalid user addresses and allocation failures terminate the faulting process.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(copyuvm skips absent PTEs so fork works with untouched heap holes. deallocuvm skips absent) Tj
T*
(leaves and frees only allocated frames. Shrinking below the original heap boundary is) Tj
T*
(rejected to protect the stack and program image. Syscall argument validation materializes) Tj
T*
(legal lazy pages before kernel I/O accesses user buffers, covering untouched read/write) Tj
T*
(buffers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(lazytest reserves 32 MB, prints free-page statistics before and after reservation, touches) Tj
T*
(four distant pages, forks across remaining holes, touches another missing page in the child,) Tj
T*
(passes an untouched page to write, and has a child access an address beyond sz. Expected:) Tj
T*
(no frame use for reservation alone; frames allocated on touch; fork survives sparse pages;) Tj
T*
(and only the invalid child is terminated.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
